                <pb facs="0274" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00/989: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Arnold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-14T14:00:00-05:56"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 15—2:11
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>32. Department’s telegram 17, September 13th, 6 p.m. Proposed conference will not
                    be held September 15th. Guatemala, Honduras, Costa Rica and Salvador have agreed
                    to place in the hands of the Central American International Bureau in Guatemala,
                    the formation of the program of the Conference as well as the fixing of the date
                    and place of the proposed conference. Nicaragua’s agreement still lacking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arnold</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
